# Vercel serves /api/* and nothing else - its root is a 404, and the dashboard
# is hosted by GitHub Pages. So the deployment needs api/ and vercel.json, and
# uploading the rest only slows the build and enlarges what is stored.
#
# The journal matters most here. It is committed every ten minutes during a
# session, and it is not read from the bundle at all: api/journal.py fetches it
# live from the GitHub contents API, which is what makes the dashboard current
# rather than as-of-last-deploy.
# pyproject.toml declares packages = ["agent", "dashboard"], and both are
# excluded below. Leaving it uploaded invites Vercel's Python builder to
# install the project and fail on packages that are not there - a build that
# fails leaves the previous deployment serving, so the site quietly keeps the
# bug the push was fixing. api/requirements.txt is the only dependency
# declaration these functions need, and it is empty on purpose.
pyproject.toml
setup.py
setup.cfg
uv.lock
poetry.lock

agent/
dashboard/
docs/
journal/
scripts/
tests/
design/
site/
.github/
.venv/
*.pptx
*.db
